== round 2 (after "keep going")
Final engine tree (prof stats2): star boards 2.5-10% productive, last level 60-80% of nodes, 88-98% of it childless;
  123_1_4657 and squares_edges ~48% productive, leaves 4-5x redundant.
Last level: of dying last-level nodes, 50-80% (star boards) have a half-edge on the NEWEST vertex with no label partner.
  -> choose_halfedge scans free half-edges newest first: A6_30 k<=8 CPU 4.7 -> 3.7 s (-22%), 1247 k<=5 -8%, s2 k<=6 -15%,
     123 k<=5 neutral; same tilings. KEPT.
Glue results cached by the pair of contexts (direct test when walks meet): validated (-DCHECK_JOINS, 9 boards, no
  mismatch) but SLOWER: A6_30 k<=8 4.4-4.7 -> 5.3-5.9 s, 123 k<=5 3.2-3.4 -> 4.4 s. Contexts + hashing cost more than the
  short face walks they replace. DROPPED.
Canonical start (prune when another root-type vertex's complete ring code beats the start's): LOSES tilings with the naive
  ring code (123 k<=4 1944 -> 1711, squares 9268 -> 9259, A6_30 1475 -> 1461): neighbour offsets depend on template
  alignment and mirror builds, so the code is not invariant. And the bound is small anyway: 0-7% fewer nodes (rings
  complete near the leaves). DROPPED.
